From 5ea4142645e477181f9dfd3ba73fdbb6b0b404f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sleepy <sleepy@example.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 11:42:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/15] drm/amd/display: merge upstream HDMI 2.1 VRR/ALLM v4
 (amdgpu-side)

Cherry-picked the three amdgpu-side patches of the HDMI 2.1 VRR + ALLM
series v4 (amd-gfx ML, 2026-08, 150622/150623/150621) that apply cleanly
to next-20260825. The drm/edid part (150619, HF-VSDB gaming caps) is
already present as our additive 0055 (functionally identical to v4 2/4).

- 1/4 amdgpu_dm_update_freesync_caps(): accept SIGNAL_TYPE_HDMI_FRL for
  AMD VSDB + emit VTEM info packet (Fangzhi Zuo) -> HDMI 2.1 FreeSync
  over FRL now works.
- 3/4 fall back to the HF-VSDB VRR range when the AMD VSDB has none
  (Fangzhi Zuo) -> HDMI compliance EDIDs report VRR-capable.
- 4/4 set ALLM_Mode in the HF-VSIF when Gaming-VRR is active per HDMI
  2.1 Sec 7.6.6 (Fangzhi Zuo).

Clean upstream replacement for the CachyOS 0107 hdmi squash, which
contributed nothing to this tree (the 7.3 base supersedes it via
dc_edid_parser + update_freesync_caps). WIP: series targets 7.4; the
4-patch group is isolated and easy to drop when it lands upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
